<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>OXBOW case packet — {{ case.case_id }} decision {{ decision.decision_seq }}</title>
<meta name="author" content="OXBOW (research prototype)">
<meta name="description" content="Append-only decision exhibit generated from persisted pipeline artifacts for a pinned run.">
<meta name="keywords" content="OXBOW, case packet, decision exhibit, audit chain, research prototype">
<meta name="generator" content="{{ packet_version }}; renderer oxbow.packet.render; typesetter WeasyPrint">
<!-- oxbow:pdf-dates -->
{{ stylesheet() }}
</head>
<body class="packet">

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ page one #}
<header class="cover">
  <p class="eyebrow">OXBOW &middot; financial-crime network intelligence &middot; case packet</p>
  <h1>Case {{ case.case_id }}</h1>
  <p class="subject-line">
    Account <span class="mono">{{ case.account_key }}</span>
    &middot; decision {{ decision.decision_seq }} of this case
    &middot; band <strong class="band band-{{ score.band }}">{{ score.band }}</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="band-figure" role="img" aria-label="Risk band {{ score.band }} of A to E, {{ band_meter.lit }} of {{ band_meter.segments_total }} meter segments lit">
    <svg class="meter" width="52" height="16" viewBox="0 0 52 16" aria-hidden="true">
      {% for segment in band_meter.segments %}
      <rect x="{{ segment.x }}" y="{{ segment.y }}" width="{{ segment.width }}" height="{{ segment.height }}"
            class="meter-segment{{ ' lit' if segment.lit else '' }}"/>
      {% endfor %}
    </svg>
    <span class="meter-letter">{{ score.band }}</span>
    <span class="meter-caption">band letter and meter glyph, so the ranking survives greyscale and a laser printer</span>
  </div>

  {# The disclaimer is on page one of every packet, verbatim (plan §15). #}
  <section class="disclaimer" id="disclaimer" aria-label="Disclaimer">
    <h2>What this document is, and what it is not</h2>
    <p class="disclaimer-text">{{ disclaimer }}</p>
    <p class="secondary">
      Account keys are salted one-way hashes produced at ingest; no raw identifier from
      any corpus appears here, and none can be recovered from it. Any East-African
      mobile-money framing in this document is illustrative scenario dressing over
      permitted public data, not a claim about any real institution, market or regulator.
      Every monetary figure in this packet is a model estimate under the assumptions
      printed in section 8, and is not a measured outcome.
    </p>
  </section>

  <table class="facts">
    <caption>Cover facts — the identifiers a reader needs to check this document against the system that produced it</caption>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Run this case is pinned to</th><td class="mono">{{ bundle.run_id }}</td>
          <td class="basis">the evidence, score, explanation and network below are this run's, as they stood at decision time</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Current run at render context</th><td class="mono">{{ runs.head_run_id }}</td>
          <td class="basis">from the run ledger; a newer run does not change this packet, which is why it is pinned</td></tr>
      {% if case.decided_on_superseded_run %}
      <tr class="flag"><th scope="row">decided_on_superseded_run</th><td class="mono">true</td>
          <td class="basis">this decision was written against a run that had <em>already</em> been superseded. The stamp is the audit row's own field, recorded inside the decision transaction, and plan §15 keeps it on the cover forever</td></tr>
      {% else %}
      <tr><th scope="row">decided_on_superseded_run</th><td class="mono">false</td>
          <td class="basis">the run was current when this decision was signed, per the audit row</td></tr>
      {% endif %}
      <tr><th scope="row">Model version</th><td class="mono">{{ score.model_version }}</td>
          <td class="basis">stamped on the scored row that produced this case</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Packet version</th><td class="mono">{{ packet_version }}</td>
          <td class="basis">layout contract, not a data version</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Decided at</th><td class="mono">{{ format_instant(decision.decided_at) }}</td>
          <td class="basis">{{ zone.label }}; recorded instant, never the render clock</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Decided by</th><td class="mono">{{ decision.actor_id }}</td>
          <td class="basis">the acting principal's subject id</td></tr>
      {% if decision.four_eyes_confirmed_by %}
      <tr><th scope="row">Four-eyes confirmed by</th><td class="mono">{{ decision.four_eyes_confirmed_by }}</td>
          <td class="basis">a second subject, required above four_eyes.threshold_exposure_minor</td></tr>
      {% endif %}
      <tr><th scope="row">Audit row covering this decision</th><td class="mono">seq={{ decision_row_seq }}</td>
          <td class="basis">chain verified on export: {{ chain_rows_checked }} rows walked, head {{ chain_head_hash }}</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Row digest / predecessor</th><td class="mono break">{{ decision_row_hash }}<br>prev {{ decision_row_prev_hash }}</td>
          <td class="basis">the digest covers the reason text, the money, the model version and this stamp</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</header>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ decision #}
<section id="decision">
  <h2>1. The decision</h2>
  <p class="decision-action"><strong>{{ decision.action }}</strong> &mdash; recorded at
    {{ format_instant(decision.decided_at) }} by <span class="mono">{{ decision.actor_id }}</span>.
    A reversal is a new row referencing the original; both appear in section 7.</p>
  <blockquote class="reason">
    <p class="reason-label">Free-text reason, as written by the reviewer (covered by the digest at seq={{ decision_row_seq }})</p>
    <p>{{ decision.reason }}</p>
  </blockquote>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ evidence #}
<section id="evidence">
  <h2>2. Evidence</h2>
  <p>{{ evidence.row_count }} canonical event(s) for
    <span class="mono">{{ evidence.account_key }}</span>, from
    <span class="mono">{{ evidence.source }}</span>, covering
    {{ format_instant(evidence.window_start) }} to {{ format_instant(evidence.window_end) }}
    ({{ zone.name }}). Ordered by the run's documented total order
    <span class="mono">(event_ts_utc, txn_id)</span>.
    {% if bundle.transaction_ids %}These are the transactions the decision named at
    signing time; the packet prints exactly those.{% endif %}</p>
  <table class="grid">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Transaction</th><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">Type</th>
          <th scope="col">Direction</th><th scope="col">Counterparty</th>
          <th scope="col">Amount (major units, ISO code)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for row in evidence.rows %}
      <tr>
        <td class="mono">{{ row.txn_id }}
          <span class="assumption-inline">column pointer: {{ row.column_pointer }}</span></td>
        <td class="mono">{{ format_instant(row.occurred_at) }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.txn_type }}</td>
        <td>{{ row.direction }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ row.counterparty }}</td>
        <td class="money">{{ row.money() | major_text(per_major) }}
          <span class="assumption-inline">observed value in {{ row.currency }}; summed per currency, never converted (no implicit FX)</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
    <tfoot>
      {% for currency, total in evidence_totals %}
      <tr><th scope="row" colspan="5">Total, {{ currency }} only</th>
        <td class="money">{{ total | minor_to_major(currency, per_major) }}
          <span class="assumption-inline">sum of the {{ currency }} rows above; an observation, not a priced estimate</span></td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tfoot>
  </table>
</section>

{# -------------------------------------------------------------------- score #}
<section id="score">
  <h2>3. Score, band and the two models' disagreement</h2>
  <table class="grid">
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Fused score</th><td class="mono">{{ '%.6f' | format(score.fused_score) }}</td>
          <td class="basis">fusion of the WOE scorecard and the gradient-boosted model, calibrated</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Band</th>
          <td class="mono">{{ score.band }} (meter {{ band_meter.lit }}/{{ band_meter.segments_total }})</td>
          <td class="basis">band letter and glyph render together; the colour is redundant decoration</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Scorecard total</th><td class="mono">{{ score.scorecard_points }} points</td>
          <td class="basis">integer points by construction, so the arithmetic is auditable by hand</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Calibrated confidence</th>
          {% if score.calibration.kind == 'uncalibrated' %}
          <td class="mono">no measured rate</td>
          <td class="basis">{{ score.calibration.note }}; the score above is this run's own
            output, and no observed rate or population was measured for the fold that produced
            it, so no confidence figure is printed in this row</td>
          {% else %}
          <td class="mono">{{ '%.4f' | format(score.calibration.observed_rate) }} observed rate on n={{ score.calibration.n }}</td>
          <td class="basis">band {{ score.calibration.band }}; n is what stops "high confidence" being an adjective</td>
          {% endif %}</tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Rules fired</th>
          <td class="mono">{% if score.rule_ids %}{{ score.rule_ids | join(', ') }}{% else %}none recorded on the scored row{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="basis">typology indicators R1–R12 (plan §9)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>3.1 Reason codes (adverse-action sentences)</h3>
  {% if score.reason_codes %}
  <ol class="reason-codes">
    {% for code in score.reason_codes %}<li>{{ code }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% else %}
  <p class="named-gap">No reason-code sentence is carried on the scored row this case
    was built from, so none is printed here. The absence is a fact about the run's
    artifacts, not a judgement about the account.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h3>3.2 Per-attribute point table</h3>
  {% if scorecard_points %}
  <table class="grid">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Attribute</th><th scope="col">Bin</th><th scope="col">Points</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for point in scorecard_points %}
      <tr><td class="mono">{{ point.feature }}</td><td>{{ point.bin_display }}</td>
          <td class="mono">{{ '%+d' | format(point.points) }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="named-gap">The per-attribute point table is not available for run
    <span class="mono">{{ bundle.run_id }}</span>: the scorecard-point handoff rows for
    that run were not on disk when this packet was composed
    (<span class="mono">out/warehouse/scorecard_point/run={{ bundle.run_id }}.jsonl</span>).
    The reason-code sentences above are the digest-covered form and are printed in full;
    this section names a gap rather than filling it.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------------- shap #}
<section id="explanation">
  <h2>4. Explanation</h2>
  <p class="source-line">
    Source: <span class="mono">{{ explanation.source }}</span>
    {% if explanation.is_scorecard_explained %}
      — <strong>scorecard-explained</strong>: the tree explanation was unavailable for
      this run ({% if explanation.fallback_reason %}{{ explanation.fallback_reason }}{% else %}the ensemble split on no feature{% endif %}),
      so the contributions below are scorecard points, not SHAP values. That is a
      different explanation, not a missing one.
    {% endif %}
    <br>Read from: <span class="mono">{{ explanation.source_pointer }}</span>.
    {{ explanation.note }}
  </p>
  <table class="grid">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Contribution</th><th scope="col">Unit</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="mono">base value</td><td class="mono">{{ '%.6f' | format(explanation.base_value) }}</td>
          <td>{{ explanation.base_unit }}</td></tr>
      {% for row in explanation.rows %}
      <tr><td class="mono">{{ row.feature }}</td><td class="mono">{{ '%+.6f' | format(row.contribution) }}</td>
          <td>{{ row.unit }}{% if row.display_value %} — {{ row.display_value }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</section>

{# ---------------------------------------------------------------- subgraph #}
<section id="network">
  <h2>5. Network neighbourhood</h2>
  <figure class="subgraph">
    {{ image.svg | safe }}
    <figcaption>{{ image.caption }}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <table class="grid per-currency">
    <caption>Value basis of the drawn edges — the line beside every currency figure in the diagram</caption>
    <tbody>
      {% for line in value_basis %}<tr><td class="basis">{{ line }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="secondary">The diagram is generated from the graph artifact by
    <span class="mono">oxbow.packet.subgraph_image</span>: concentric hop rings, node type
    by shape, value by stroke weight, events by the <span class="mono">Nx CUR</span> marks.
    It is not a screenshot of the explorer, so it can be reproduced from the rows it depicts.
    Rails (square nodes) are endpoints and are never traversed through, which is why a rail
    in the middle of a path does not connect the accounts either side of it.</p>
</section>

{# ---------------------------------------------------------------- economics #}
<section id="economics">
  <h2>6. What reviewing this account is worth</h2>
  <p>Every figure below is printed with the assumption line beside it (plan §11, §15).
    Money is integer minor units carried through the whole pipeline and divided at
    render time only, so the totals above and the figures here reconcile.</p>
  <table class="grid money-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">Amount</th><th scope="col">Basis of this figure</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for line in money_lines %}
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">{{ line.label }}</th>
        <td class="money">{{ line.render() }}</td>
        <td class="basis">{{ line.basis }}
          <span class="assumption-inline">Assumption keys: {{ assumption_keys }} — verbatim block in section 8</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="secondary">Not shown as a band: <span class="mono">EV_i</span> is printed at
    the recovery rate this decision was actually priced at
    (r={{ economics_block.recovery_rate }}), because recomputing it would need
    <span class="mono">p_i</span>, which the decision bundle does not carry. The
    <span class="mono">E_i x r</span> row is the only figure restated over the band, and
    it is a multiplication of a recorded exposure, not a re-run of the model.</p>
</section>

{# ----------------------------------------------------------------- timeline #}
<section id="timeline">
  <h2>7. Append-only decision log for this case</h2>
  <p>Both a decision and any reversal of it appear, each with the digest that covers it.
    Nothing in this table is an edit of an earlier row — mutation is what would destroy
    the integrity claim this packet is built on.</p>
  <table class="grid">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">seq</th><th scope="col">When ({{ zone.name }})</th><th scope="col">Action</th>
      <th scope="col">Actor</th><th scope="col">Reason</th><th scope="col">Row digest</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for entry in timeline %}
      <tr class="{{ 'flag' if entry.decided_on_superseded_run else '' }}">
        <td class="mono">{{ entry.seq }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ format_instant(entry.occurred_at) }}</td>
        <td>{{ entry.action_verb }}{% if entry.reversal_of_seq is not none %} of seq {{ entry.reversal_of_seq }}{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ entry.actor_id }}</td>
        <td>{{ entry.reason }}</td>
        <td class="mono break">{{ entry.row_hash }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="integrity">Chain verification on export: <strong>{{ chain_rows_checked }} rows
    walked and every digest recomputed</strong>; head
    <span class="mono break">{{ chain_head_hash }}</span>. The walk happened during this
    render and the render carries no render-time clock: the document's own dates are the
    recorded instants in the table above.</p>
</section>

{# ------------------------------------------------------------- assumptions #}
<section id="assumptions">
  <h2>8. Assumptions, verbatim</h2>
  <p>Reprinted from <span class="mono">{{ assumptions.source_path }}</span> by
    <span class="mono">oxbow.quant.economics.assumption_block()</span> — the same text the
    product renders under a currency figure and the same text
    <span class="mono">oxbow eval</span> publishes, so a figure cannot meet a shorter
    version of its own assumptions in one surface than another.</p>
  <pre class="assumptions">{{ assumptions.text }}</pre>
  <p class="secondary">Keys named by every money line in this document:
    <span class="mono">{{ assumption_keys }}</span>.
    Changing a value in that file changes every figure in section 6; that is the point of
    printing them together.</p>
</section>

{# -------------------------------------------------------------- provenance #}
<section id="provenance">
  <h2>9. Provenance</h2>
  <ul class="provenance mono">
    <li>decision bundle (spine of this document): the case-sink payload for
        <span>{{ bundle.run_id }} / {{ case.case_id }} / decision {{ decision.decision_seq }}</span></li>
    <li>evidence: {{ evidence.source }}</li>
    <li>network drawing: {{ subgraph.source }}</li>
    <li>explanation: {{ explanation.source_pointer }}</li>
    <li>assumptions: {{ assumptions.source_path }}</li>
    <li>run ledger: {{ runs.head_run_id }} as head of {{ runs.runs | length }} recorded run(s)</li>
    <li>audit chain: {{ chain_rows_checked }} rows, covering digest at seq {{ decision_row_seq }}</li>
    <li>rendering: {{ packet_version }}, typeset by WeasyPrint; fonts
        <span>{{ fonts.sans }}</span> / <span>{{ fonts.mono }}</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="secondary">Every account identifier above is a salted one-way hash from
    ingest (config/sources.yaml :: deidentification.account_key). Re-identification
    requires the run salt, which is not in this document, not in the packet directory,
    and not in the repository.</p>
</section>

<footer class="endnote">
  <p>{{ disclaimer }}</p>
  <p class="mono">packet {{ packet_version }} &middot; case {{ case.case_id }} &middot;
    decision {{ decision.decision_seq }} &middot; run {{ bundle.run_id }} &middot;
    audit seq {{ decision_row_seq }} &middot; {{ format_instant(decision.decided_at) }}</p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
